  "id": "COMPOUND:23663 - PROTEIN:1502",
  "verbalization": "Phellandral, (R)- is consistently identified as a target of CDK3/Cyclin E, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 2-(5-Hydroxy-1H-Indol-3-Yl)Acetic Acid and Kutzneride 9. All these compounds ultimately direct their activity to Extracellular signal-regulated kinase (ERK). This suggests a mechanistic pathway where Phellandral, (R)- indirectly influences ERK through the CDK3/Cyclin E pathway. The evidence is robust, with multiple independent pathways converging on the same target hierarchy, indicating a well-defined relationship. The integration of these findings supports the notion that Phellandral, (R)- may act through a CDK3/Cyclin E-dependent mechanism that ultimately leads to ERK activation. The presence of multiple targets in the CDK3/Cyclin E pathway further strengthens the hypothesis that Phellandral, (R)- exerts its effects via this route.",
